WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.720
In the UK in 2024,

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.060
the gender pay gap for
full-time workers aged 22

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:09.580
to 29 was 1.3 per cent.

4
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:12.250
For full-time workers aged 60 and over,

5
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:15.190
it was 13.5 per cent.

6
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:18.140
But a gap is not all discrimination.

7
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.440
Hours, jobs and career breaks differ too.

8
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.170
So if two workers are equally productive,

9
00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.010
how can one still end up paid less?

10
00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:30.340
In this mission, you'll see
how economists test employers

11
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:34.480
with job applications that are
identical except for a name.

12
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.740
Then you'll use a graph
lab to measure what

13
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.690
prejudice costs one group of workers.

14
00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:44.670
Your mission: explain how equally
productive workers can end up paid less.
